Title: Pre-commit guard: refuse direct commits on main in the primary checkout
Created: 2026-06-06
Author: Integration Test

--- log ---
2026-06-06T14:58Z Integration Test created

--- body ---
## Context

During the 2026-06-06 raid the primary checkout (~/.claude) was found
DIVERGED: a dream session had committed e3dfb27 (memory consolidation)
directly to local main without push or PR — violating the
everything-via-PR rule and silently starving every skill resolution of
13 upstream commits (merged gaze mechanism changes were inert until
the orchestrator noticed and synced). Rescued via branch + PR #334.
Failure family matches feedback_beat_checkout_model (skills operating
on a main checkout). The session-level PreToolUse guard does not fire
for sessions legitimately rooted in the primary repo.

## Actions

1. Extend hooks/pre-commit (repo-side, fires regardless of session
   type): refuse a commit when HEAD is main in the PRIMARY checkout
   (worktrees excluded — branch commits there are the normal flow;
   also exclude rebase/merge-in-progress states and CI).
   Override: ALLOW_MAIN_COMMIT=1 for deliberate cases.
2. Audit skills that run on the primary checkout (dream, beat,
   nightbeat) for commit steps lacking a branch guard; fix the texts.
3. Prove RED: a test commit on main in a scratch clone is refused.

## Test

hooks/pre-commit refuses `git commit` on main in the primary checkout
and allows the same commit on a branch; existing suites stay green.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Pre-commit guard refuses direct main commits (override env var documented)
- [ ] dream/beat/nightbeat texts audited; unguarded commit steps fixed
- [ ] RED/GREEN proof in PR body
- [ ] make check passes
